/* ==================================================================
   S C O P ' D
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   Black Ops II  //  Cronus Zen / GPC                     v4.5
   SNIPER BUILD  -  OFFLINE / BOT LOBBY / CAMPAIGN
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   MENU        : hold L2 + tap OPTIONS
   MASTER KILL : hold L2 + tap SHARE
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v4.5 - 540/720 TIERS FOR AXE/RLD/MEL/TEMPER/BARREL

   YY180, YY1080, YYY720, YY2360, YY2720, JMPYY, DRPMEL, YY3360,
   YY3720, RUN1080 removed to make room (10 slots - none of them were
   in any default bind, checked before touching anything). In their
   place: AXE540/AXE720, RLD540/RLD720, MEL540/MEL720, TMP540/TMP720,
   BAR540/BAR720 - the missing middle tiers between each trick's 360
   version and its v4.4 1080 version. Every family (AXE/RLD/MEL/TMP/
   BAR) now has 360, 540, 720, and 1080 all available.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v4.4 - FIVE NEW 1080 TRICKS

   RUNJMP, RUN720, DIV360, DIV720, DIVYY (dive/run tricks) removed to
   make room. In their place: AXE1080, RLD1080, MEL1080, TMP1080 (the
   TEMPER jump+YY+swap-finish shape at 1080 instead of 360), BAR1080
   (BARREL's swap-pre+YY shape at 1080). Same fields as their 360
   counterparts, SPIN bumped to the 1080 enum value. No other slot
   moved - default binds only ever pointed at 2/4/6/8/16/19/22/29,
   none of which were touched.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v4.3 - PAGE COUNTER FIX, XTRA DOWN, TS AUTO

   Page header was showing "14/12": the "/N" total was never a real
   number, it was two hardcoded characters '1' and '2' left over from
   when there were 12 pages. Both halves of the counter render off
   the real page numbers now.

   STEAL EMBLEM gained XTRA DOWN (0-6, default 4): extra DOWN presses
   tacked onto the base 2 at the end of the sequence. This needed the
   macro to stop being a combo - combos can't loop or branch, and a
   runtime-variable repeat count needs both - so it's now a small
   tick-driven sequencer (se_start/se_run) instead, same pattern the
   trickshot engine already uses for its own windows.

   SYSTEM gained TS AUTO: loads the tested TS TIMING baseline (TAP
   28, GAP 24, STAGE 7, LEAD 0, PRE 8, FIN 4, TAIL 6) in one press
   instead of resetting seven lines by hand with TRIANGLE. It's the
   documented starting point, not a live calibration - CALIBRATE's
   FIRE TEST / APPLY FIX / TUNE GAP is still what actually tunes it
   to your setup from there.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v4.2 - STEAL EMBLEM TAB

   New page, nothing else touched. STEAL EMBLEM is a fixed menu-
   navigation sequence for the Barracks emblem-copy glitch - X,
   Circle x3, X, X, Down x2 - fired by a bindable trigger (L3/R3/L1/
   R1) while ENABLE is on, with its own TAP/GAP timing since a menu's
   input window behaves nothing like a match's. FIRE TEST runs it
   once from the menu for tuning. It's a straight combo, not the
   trickshot sequencer - the sequence is fixed length and strictly
   serial, nothing to overlap.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v4.1 - SLOT EDIT ACTUALLY SAVES NOW

   PG_SLOT (the page id slot_sync() gates on) was defined as 4, which
   is CALIBRATE - SLOT EDIT is page 3. slot_sync() only ever runs
   "if(m_page == PG_SLOT)", so with the wrong id it silently did
   nothing the entire time you were on the real SLOT EDIT page: your
   PRE 1 / PRE 2 / CANCEL 1-4 / SPIN / FINISH edits changed the number
   on screen (that's just oval[]) but never touched ts_slot[], so
   firing SLOTA-D always played whatever ts_slot[] already held, and
   SAVE ALL / CIRCLE-to-exit wrote that same untouched data back out.
   Selecting a different slot in EDIT SLOT didn't reload its fields
   either, for the same reason. One-line fix: PG_SLOT = 3.

   Also corrected O_SL_CAN3's default (ODEF) to YY, matching SLOTDEF
   A's actual third cancel - it had drifted to NONE, which only ever
   showed up if you pressed TRIANGLE to reset that one line.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v4.0 - SNIPER ONLY, AIM PRECISION REBUILT, FOUR CANCELS

   Every option that wasn't sniping or trickshotting is gone: SNAP
   AIM, SCOPE BAIT, SEMI AUTO (rapid fire + anti-recoil) and HAIR
   TRIGGER are deleted outright, not just hidden. That's 15 pages
   down to 12, and every remaining page earns its place.

   AIM ASSIST is not the same feature anymore. CIRCLE / PULSE /
   STRAFE were stick-wiggle patterns injected on top of your real
   input regardless of whether you were also moving it - which is
   what "tweaking" on small corrections actually was. It's replaced
   by three things that shape YOUR input instead of fighting it:
     CURVE   - precision near centre, speed further out
     SMOOTH  - low-pass filter that kills hand tremor / micro-jitter
     BREATH LINK - both tighten automatically while breath is held
   plus an optional, small, heavily-suppressed MICRO NUDGE for
   anyone who still wants a magnetism-style pull - off by default.

   SLOT EDIT goes to FOUR cancel stages (was three), because there
   was never a real reason it should have had fewer cancels than
   pre-moves and finishers had headroom for. To make room without
   breaking the two-pvar / 3-bit-per-field save packing, FINISH
   drops from two fields to one - with a new composite "PR+MEL"
   value so a PRONE-then-MELEE ending (MONSTR, DRPMEL) still works
   in a single field. Every existing macro re-expresses cleanly in
   the new 8-field shape: 2 PRE, 4 CANCEL, 1 SPIN, 1 FINISH.

   Pages reordered: AIM ASSIST stays 1, then TRICKSHOT (2), TS
   TIMING (3), SLOT EDIT (4), TS BINDS (5), TS BINDS+ (6) - the
   sequencer is now front and centre instead of buried on page 9.
   TURBO MELEE moved from the deleted TRIGGERS page into MOVEMENT,
   which otherwise keeps everything it had.

   OLED: boot and idle no longer print "SCOP'D" or draw the rule
   line under it - idle is eyes only now, always, no more SCOPE /
   BINDS / CYCLE views. That runner-simulation scene, the bind
   preview screen and their support code are gone along with the
   IDLE VIEW option.

   BREAKING: this is enough of a structural change to the save
   format (new fields, deleted fields, different slot packing) that
   trying to migrate every old value field-by-field was more risk
   than it was worth getting quietly wrong. v4.0 resets ALL saved
   settings on first load, once - not just the four custom slots as
   past layout changes have done. Re-tune TS TIMING and re-bind your
   directions after the first boot on this version.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v3.2 - AIM ASSIST STOPPED FIGHTING SMALL CORRECTIONS

   The assist offset (CIRCLE/PULSE/STRAFE) was being added straight on
   top of the real right-stick value with no regard for whether the
   player was also moving it. A full-power assist vector stacked on a
   tiny manual nudge is what "tweaking" on small aim adjustments was -
   the offset dominated the input instead of assisting it. Superseded
   by the v4.0 aim precision rebuild above.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v3.1 - EIGHT FIELDS

   v3.0 gave a trickshot four named sections, which fixed the flow but
   allowed exactly ONE cancel. Long shots need more: a running jump
   buys close to a second of airtime and you want two or three cancels
   inside it, spaced differently from the taps inside each one.

   So a trickshot is eight fields now:

       PRE 1     PRE 2     CANCEL 1  CANCEL 2
       CANCEL 3  SPIN      FINISH 1  FINISH 2

   PRE 2 exists mainly for SPRINT + JUMP. Sprint deliberately stays
   held past the point the jump fires, so the jump goes off while you
   are still running - a running jump, which is the higher, longer one
   with room for the extra cancels.

   And GAP split in two. GAP is the rhythm INSIDE one cancel; STAGE is
   the rest between one cancel and the next. One number could not
   express "tight YY, loose spacing between cancels", which is what a
   multi-cancel shot actually needs.

   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v3.0 - SECTIONED TRICKSHOTS

   v2 made the spin parallel but still laid the button presses end to
   end, and it stored a slot as eight loose "steps" - so a jump shot
   was jump, wait, swap, wait, swap, and nothing overlapped except the
   stick. That is what "not smooth" was.

   v3 gives every trickshot four named sections that deliberately
   overlap in time:

       PRE      jump / dive / swap-out / prone / crouch / sprint
       CANCEL   YY / YYY / YYYY / reload / axe / melee / tac
       SPIN     180 .. 1080, off one calibrated SPIN 360ms
       FINISH   prone / melee / swap / crouch / jump / reload

   CANCEL starts PRE x10 INTO the pre-move rather than after it, so
   the YY lands while you are still coming off the jump. FINISH fires
   FIN x10 after whichever of CANCEL and SPIN ends last. The library
   macros are just named presets over those four fields (MACDEF[]),
   and the four custom slots compose the same four fields by hand.

   The spin also has an envelope now - whip out, carry, settle - so it
   stops looking like a switch. SPIN RAMP sets the depth, and the
   window is lengthened by exactly the area the envelope gives up, so
   the rotation stays calibrated at every setting.

   NOTHING TOUCHES L2 OR R2. No auto-scope, no auto-fire. The macro
   choreographs the movement and the cancels; you scope and you shoot.

   Every gap is tunable on TS TIMING - see the README.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   GPC NOTES: no local variables - all working vars are top level,
   prefixed by owner. Combos take set_val/wait only, no branching,
   which is exactly why the sequencer lives in a function instead.
   print() takes a data-section address, not a literal; no %d.

   SCREEN BUDGET (128 x 64, small font 7px wide / 8px tall):
     header y 0..11 | rows y 15,25,35,45,55 | labels x 3 (10 chars)
     values x 76 (6 chars) | scrollbar x 121..125
   ================================================================== */


/* ---------------- BUTTON LAYOUT (edit me) ---------------- */
define BTN_FIRE    = PS4_R2;
define BTN_ADS     = PS4_L2;
